"""
=============================================================================
qica_v7.py  —  Multi-Entropy QICA  |  Calibrated Shannon Entropy  [FIXED]
=============================================================================
Carries forward all v6 fixes (trust-region trajectory entropy, h_rank source,
AL dedup) and fixes the THREE problems found in the v6 run:

WHAT WENT WRONG IN v6, AND WHY
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PROBLEM 1 — H_hist collapsed to ≈0.000 for almost every pattern
  v6 used a FIXED bin range taken from the *training-data PPF spread*
  (1.78–5.54, bin width 0.376). But actual MC-dropout spread per pattern is
  only σ≈0.05–0.10. Every pattern's 30 MC samples land inside ONE bin of
  that 0.376-wide grid → H≈0 for nearly everyone.
  This is the mirror image of the ORIGINAL bug (per-pattern local bins made
  H≈2.3 for everyone) — both versions picked a bin window disconnected from
  the actual noise scale, just in opposite directions.

  FIX 6: Center each pattern's MC samples on its OWN mean (removes the
  across-pattern PPF-LEVEL spread, which is irrelevant to uncertainty), then
  bin into a FIXED window calibrated from the ACTUAL MC sigma scale
  (measured once via a calibration pass): half_width ≈ 4×typical_σ. This
  keeps entropy comparable across patterns and generations (fixed bins,
  needed for the population/AL-threshold logic to be stable) while making
  bin width comparable to the real noise scale.

PROBLEM 2 — AL candidates = 0 for the entire run
  Direct consequence of Problem 1: AL_HIST_THRESHOLD=0.7 is a value tuned
  for a different (broken) entropy scale, so it was never crossed.

  FIX 7: AL flagging is now PURELY adaptive — it uses a percentile of the
  current batch's H_hist among low-PPF candidates (default: top 30% most
  uncertain), so it self-calibrates to whatever the entropy scale actually
  is each run, instead of relying on a hand-tuned absolute number.

PROBLEM 3 — optimizer stuck at PPF≈1.94–2.01 for ~200 generations
  v6's stagnation injection always reseeded from the SINGLE best elite with
  a FIXED mutation strength/count, so the population kept getting pulled
  straight back into the same basin every 15 generations instead of
  escaping it.

  FIX 8: Escalating, multi-elite stagnation injection. Seeds are drawn
  round-robin from the top-3 elites (not just rank 1), and both the
  mutation strength (number of randomized positions) and batch size grow
  with the number of CONSECUTIVE stagnation rounds — so each escape attempt
  is more aggressive than the last, instead of repeating forever. The
  escalation counter resets the moment a genuinely better fitness is found.

H_traj (trajectory entropy) was already working correctly in v6 — untouched.

INPUTS:   cnn_v9_model.keras, cnn_v9_config.json, train_type_freq_v9.npy
OUTPUTS:  qica_v7_best_patterns.csv, qica_v7_al_candidates.csv,
          qica_v7_convergence.png, qica_v7_entropy_comparison.png
=============================================================================
"""

